#X obj 638 8 conv.bits2note;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 206 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 The object takes a list of bits (0s and 1s) and turns
each bit into a note event \, using the note numbers provided in the
KEYS argument (or the @keys property). In the default mode each bit
corresponds to its own outlet \, and a pair (NOTE VEL) is sent to that
outlet. If the bit is 1 \, the velocity is @vel; if the bit is 0 \,
the velocity is 0 (note off).;
#X text 240 199 In @poly mode a single outlet is used \, and instead
of a (NOTE VEL) pair a (VOICE NOTE VEL) triplet is sent — this is convenient
for use with the [clone] object \, where VOICE identifies the clone
instance.;
